      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/e106ac16-6c64-4f45-b918-9145fd393f7c)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality \u0026 Security:**\n- The CL successfully attempts to address multiplication integer overflow issues in `sys_alloc`, but introduces a secondary integer overflow vulnerability when computing the final allocation size (`hdr_size + total`). If `total` is close to `SIZE_MAX`, this addition can wrap around, leading to a much smaller allocation than requested while recording a large size in the chunk header (which results in a heap buffer overflow).\n- `plat_calloc` has inconsistent overflow handling compared to `sys_alloc`. While `sys_alloc` will panic (`k_oops()`) on overflow, `plat_calloc` now returns `NULL`. The overflow logic in `plat_calloc` also duplicates checks already performed in `sys_alloc`.\n\n**Style \u0026 Consistency:**\n- The code changes are clear and adhere to standard project style. Using `sys_alloc` and `sys_alloc_usable_size` directly inside `plat_calloc` will improve consistency and simplify the codebase.\n\n**Testing:**\n- Existing testing configurations appear to be executed, but no new unit tests have been added for the integer overflow edge cases.",
