      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a potential integer overflow when adding `hdr_size` to `total`. If `total` is very large (e.g., close to `SIZE_MAX`), `hdr_size + total` can wrap around to a small value. This would cause `k_heap_aligned_alloc` to allocate a small buffer, while the header records the large `total` size, leading to a heap buffer overflow when the caller uses the returned buffer.\n\nConsider using `__builtin_add_overflow` to check for overflow before allocating:\n```c\n\tsize_t alloc_size;\n\tif (__builtin_add_overflow(total, hdr_size, \u0026alloc_size)) {\n\t\tLOG_ERR(\"Error - allocation size overflows.\");\n\t\tk_oops();\n\t\tCODE_UNREACHABLE;\n\t}\n\tuint8_t *raw \u003d k_heap_aligned_alloc(\u0026fp_driver_heap, ALIGNMENT,\n\t\t\t\t\t    alloc_size, K_NO_WAIT);\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "9242a71d8c4b24c4822650bbcce48e090718fbf5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
